-- Resolves the signup half of rovno audit #186 (vladosda0/rovno): the UI boots
-- Russian (i18n defaults to ru) but public.profiles.locale defaulted to 'en', so
-- every account created through signup disagreed with the language it was
-- actually shown. The signup handler public.handle_auth_user_created
-- (20260522130200:131-146, confirmed to be its last redefinition) inserts only
-- (id, email, full_name, avatar_url) and never sets locale, so the column
-- default is the sole governor of a new user's locale. Aligning the default to
-- the product's real default language fixes new signups at the source.
--
-- The existing CHECK (locale in ('ru','en','de','fr')) already admits 'ru', so no
-- constraint change is needed. Verified against the live catalog rather than
-- inferred, this is pg_get_constraintdef verbatim:
--   CHECK ((locale = ANY (ARRAY['ru'::text, 'en'::text, 'de'::text, 'fr'::text])))
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Scope: the DEFAULT ONLY. There is deliberately NO backfill.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- An earlier revision also ran `update public.profiles set locale = 'ru' where
-- locale = 'en'`. Pre-merge review found that backfill to be the sole cause of
-- three separate problems, so it was dropped rather than patched:
--
--   1. It re-aimed a pre-existing frontend bug onto a new cohort.
--      ProfilePanel.handleSave (ProfilePanel.tsx:153-155) calls
--      setAppLanguage(language) on EVERY successful save, where `language` was
--      seeded from user.locale and is untouched when the user edits only their
--      name, phone, bio, signature, timezone or avatar. A SECOND interface
--      language control (PreferencesPanel.tsx:65-70, «Язык интерфейса») and a
--      THIRD (OnboardingStepper.tsx:47-49) write localStorage ONLY and never
--      profiles.locale. So a user with locale='ru' who had chosen English in
--      Предпочтения would be silently and permanently flipped back to Russian by
--      saving anything at all in Профиль. The bug is pre-existing and symmetric
--      (today it mis-fires on the Russian-speaking majority instead), but a
--      backfill newly breaks the English cohort, and that trade is not this
--      migration's to make.
--   2. Its WHERE clause was inverted relative to its own rationale. The
--      justification was that 'en' reflects the old default rather than a
--      deliberate choice, but 'en' IS selectable, whereas 'de'/'fr'/'es' are
--      `disabled: true` in LANGUAGES (ProfilePanel.tsx:33-38) and therefore
--      strictly unselectable, so only a de/fr row is certain to be accidental. It
--      flipped the possibly-deliberate values and spared the provably-accidental
--      ones.
--   3. It was not idempotent in effect. The ALTER below is; a re-run of that
--      UPDATE silently reverted deliberate English choices made in between. That
--      matters here because prod applies with `db push --include-all`, the Studio
--      SQL Editor path does not record in schema_migrations, and a prior incident
--      applied uncommitted migrations from a dirty worktree.
--
-- Consequence of shipping the default alone: existing rows keep whatever locale
-- they have, and every NEW signup is correct. Existing 'en' rows keep today's
-- mismatch until #186's remaining half (a single source of truth for interface
-- language) is addressed separately.
--
-- This is a TRADE, not a free win, and the earlier revision of this header wrongly
-- claimed "nothing regresses for anyone". The bug described in point 1 above is
-- symmetric, so moving the default moves which cohort it bites:
--
--   * REMOVED (large): today a new RU user gets locale='en' from the old default,
--     picks Russian in Предпочтения, then saves anything in Профиль and is flipped
--     to English. That is the majority case and it stops happening.
--   * ADDED (small): a new user who gets locale='ru' from this default, picks
--     English in Предпочтения, then saves anything in Профиль is flipped to
--     Russian. On the old default that user's DB value matched their choice, so no
--     flip occurred.
--
-- Net affected population shrinks and the DB default now agrees with i18n's boot
-- default, which is why this ships. The root defect (an unconditional
-- setAppLanguage plus two competing controls for one setting) is untouched here and
-- tracked separately.
--
-- Blast radius: none beyond new rows. profiles.locale is read from the database
-- at src/data/workspace-source.ts:703/750/833 -> mapProfileRowToUser:426 ->
-- user.locale, and consumed only by ProfilePanel.tsx:76/86/111/169.
-- (src/lib/auth-state.ts:169 and src/data/store.ts:89 mirror a localStorage copy
-- for local/demo mode; they do not read this table.) No edge function selects the
-- column, and the AI answer language comes from
-- profile_settings.ai_output_language via ai-inference, not from here.
--
-- Idempotent, and curated-ALLOWLISTED: the backend-truth parser gained an
-- `alter column ... set default` handler in the same change, so the generated
-- mirror now reflects this default instead of silently reporting the old one.

alter table public.profiles
  alter column locale set default 'ru';
